  logEntries:
  - The keeper's cottage at the foot of the mountain is a ruin. The path starts on the beach and winds up and around, and it never once turns back.
  - The gaps in the path were not made by the weather. Someone took the stones out on purpose, and crossed them on bridges of light.
  - At the very top stands the Great Light, dark for as long as anyone remembers. Eight beacons wake it. I have lit none. Not yet.
  introLines:
  - One path climbs the mountain, round and round. Follow it to the top.
  - Some gaps are too wide to cross. Light the beacon at the edge and a bridge of light will carry you over.
  - The higher you climb, the harder the storm. It never eases again, even if you turn back.
  - Light all eight beacons. Then the Great Light.
